{
  // Typecheck-only config for `prisma/` — the seed and its seed-data modules.
  //
  // WHY THIS EXISTS AS A SECOND CONFIG
  // ----------------------------------
  // `tsconfig.json` sets `"rootDir": "src"` because it BUILDS the package, so
  // adding `prisma` to its `include` fails with TS6059 ("not under rootDir")
  // rather than typechecking anything. Widening the build's rootDir to reach a
  // script that is never compiled into `dist/` would change what the package
  // emits, to fix a checking gap.
  //
  // WHAT THE GAP WAS
  // ----------------
  // `prisma/seed.ts` was typechecked by nothing. Office-scoped custom roles
  // made `Role` require `organizationId`/`nameAr`/`nameEn` and moved its unique
  // key to `(organizationId, name)`; the seed still wrote the old shape, and
  // `npm run typecheck` passed 6/6 across the whole monorepo while the seed
  // could not run at all. CI caught it — in the one step no local gate covers,
  // on a database fresh enough to need a CREATE rather than an upsert-existing.
  //
  // The seed is the only thing CI runs that nothing typechecks, and every
  // remaining phase of this rework touches both the schema and the seed. One
  // extra `tsc` invocation turns that class of failure from a CI round-trip
  // into a local error.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "rootDir": ".",
    // The seed and its spec run under tsx/vitest, which resolve ESM-style
    // relative imports and JSON; the build's commonjs settings are irrelevant
    // to a file that is never emitted.
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  "include": ["prisma"]
}
